description:
FILED + FIXED s518e (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-17) from the Type-Tiny census.

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs main 5c5a5679):

    package Q; sub m { "m:" . ref(shift) } package main;
    eval q{ *P::f = sub { bless {}, "Q" }; 1 } or die;
    print P::f()->m, "\n";

perl `m:Q`; PCL dies `Can't locate object method "m" via package "P::f"`.  Emission `(p-method-call (p-resolve-invocant "P::f") "m")`: the funcall node does not keep its parens, and p-resolve-invocant looked the name up UNQUALIFIED in the current package only.

=== DONE (s518e) ===
cl/pcl-runtime.lisp p-resolve-invocant: a QUALIFIED name with no package of that name is a call when the sub exists, through the ONE resolver (p-get-coderef); a known package stays a class (perl's order).  Guard Pl/t/universal-01.t row 10 (perl oracle: also `Known::Cls->m` with a sub of that name, and `No::Such()->m` dies), fails on main.  NOT done: the parser still drops the `()` that makes perl call even when a package of that name exists (no case seen).
